    <string name="repair_launcher_unknown">unknown launcher</string>
    <string name="repair_body">A "Can\'t load widget" cell has two possible causes:\n\n1. The widget is bound to this app but its view is broken. The button below immediately pushes a brand-new view to every bound widget — that fixes this case, no network needed.\n\n2. The cell is dead data left in the launcher\'s own memory (%1$s) and is bound to nothing: no app can repair it. Remove it by hand (long-press the cell → Remove), then add the widget again.\n\nWhen in doubt: reboot the phone, put the widget back, tap it to set it up. This app\'s list only shows widgets that are actually configured; leftover "ghost bindings" are counted in the Diagnostics panel and will go away on their own after a launcher restart.</string>
    <string name="repair_open">Open launcher info</string>
    <string name="repair_line">"Can\'t load widget": try "Repair / repaint" first; if the cell stays broken it\'s dead launcher data → remove it by hand.</string>

